  /* ============================================================
     PHASE 7.1 — PRODUCTS "CATALOG MARGINS v2" DOODLE LAYER
     Page-specific 8-doodle map at Club Hub scale (revised from the too-
     small Phase 7.0 placement proof). Zones (all measured @1440, abs):
     HEADER — two large marks flanking the giant KID logo (logo x631-812
     y39-221; nav row 1 starts y254; fixed cart x>=1350 @1440, left edge
     ~x1104 @1200 — both header marks verified clear at both extremes).
     MARGINS — outer strips; base size fits 1280's 89px card edge, with a
     >=1366px bump (card edge 111 @1366 / 129 @1440); ink MAY cross the
     red/blue vertical rules (like real margin scribbles) but never card
     boxes. GUTTER — the clean center channel between the product columns
     (shadow-cleared lane 129px @1366 / 166px @1440), >=1366px only.
     BOTTOM — two strong marks on the CTA flanks, BOTTOM-ANCHORED in the
     constant ~219px band between grid end and page end (both ends move
     together under title-wrap/font variation, so the band never shrinks);
     CTA x602-838, copyright ~x660-780, cart max-scroll band x>=1350 —
     all cleared. Layering: wrapper absolute inset:0 / z-index:0 inside
     #MainContent, rendered BEFORE the product-grid section, so the grid
     paints above it — no z-lift needed; v3 img shadows untouched.
     Page-anchored on purpose (glued to the scrolling paper; NOT
     viewport-fixed — fixed ink would slide across the ruled lines).
     Ink treatment per the accepted Life/Style learning (blend normal +
     per-doodle darkening). Star is the ONLY duplicated asset: header
     star large/upright vs bottom star ~35% smaller + scaleX(-1) mirrored
     + different rotation, per the duplicate-doodle rule.
     aria-hidden / pointer-events:none / hidden <1200px (gutter pair
     additionally <1366px).
